{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Awaken.</b> The cup of His wrath — by way of parable, like a man who becomes drunk and does not know what is done to him, and he lies asleep." "<b>Pierced.</b> It has no [such] meaning. Some say: the dregs that settle at the bottom." "<b>The reeling.</b> Like והברושים הורעלו (Nahum 2:4) — like a shudder that a man shudders upon seeing it." "<b>You have drained.</b> From the root of למען תמצו (Isaiah 66:11). And if they are two roots, the meaning is complete chastisement."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {3 "The bracketed editorial correction [צ\"ל שרשים] reads: 'read: roots,' correcting what appears in the witnesses as שנים בנינים ('two binyanim'). Translated the corrected reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:05.655725545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}